### A person signing in from a browser — POST, GET, DELETE /api/v1/session
# What each operation takes, answers and refuses:
# ../contracts/in/web-session-api.md

@host = http://localhost:1000
# Set from the XSRF-TOKEN cookie the "read the session" request below returns; every write needs it.
@csrfToken = paste-the-XSRF-TOKEN-cookie-value-here
# Set from the fb_session cookie the sign-in response sets.
@sessionCookie = paste-the-fb_session-cookie-value-here

### Sign in — opens a session. The body is exactly what the Telegram Login Widget hands the page, hash
### included; paste a real payload rather than editing these fields, since the hash covers every one of them.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/session
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: XSRF-TOKEN={{csrfToken}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{
  "id": "123456789",
  "auth_date": "1700000000",
  "hash": "the-widget's-hash-over-every-other-field"
}

### Read the session — answers who the browser is signed in as. Run this once, unauthenticated, to obtain the
### XSRF-TOKEN cookie the sign-in above needs; a read itself needs no CSRF token.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/session
Cookie: fb_session={{sessionCookie}}

### End the session — clears it, whether or not one was open.
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/session
Cookie: fb_session={{sessionCookie}}; XSRF-TOKEN={{csrfToken}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}
